 "verdict": "HOLD THE WEEKLY SLOT. H-38 fails the blocked SGMC-proxy gate (0/5 folds vs random at both budgets: 1.22% mean DTI 0.0075 / 0.0494 lidar-gated vs random 0.0995) AND shows null or negative live-score consistency (Spearman rho = -0.0600, lidar-gated rho = -0.3339 with |G|=10k log-skill). H-39 also fails the blocked SGMC-proxy gate as a standalone emission (0/5 folds vs random: 1.22% mean DTI 0.0151 / 0.0174 thick-cover vs random 0.0995); although its live-score correlation is positive (rho = +0.3904 for 500 m residual edges, +0.3261 for thick-cover; top-4 minus rest = +0.0902 / +0.0966 log units), in the 15-fold leave-one-family-out habitat nested-CV follow-up it ranks 37-50/96 by univariate |Spearman| (well below the k=8 cutoff 0.5548 and k=14 cutoff 0.5070), is selected in 0/15 folds (unforced CV unchanged at 0.437391), and degrades CV when the raw layer is force-appended (0.383478, delta = -0.053913 at |G|=6,000) while the [0,1]-normalized layer shifts CV by only +0.008696 (0.446087, k=8, beta = +0.2726) at |G|=6,000 and -0.024348 at |G|=15,000. Both H-38 and H-39 are therefore closed and neither is emitted into a submission raster."
}
